re the first position.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"EliasFanoGraph.Edges.Iterator","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/eliasfanographmodule\/eliasfanograph\/edges-swift.struct\/iterator","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Iterator"}]},"doc://EliasFanoGraphModule/documentation/EliasFanoGraphModule/EliasFanoGraph/Edges-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"The edges of a graph, or a contiguous run of them. Positions are edge indices. Iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decodes each row once, O(1) amortized per edge; subscripting one position is O(log n +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-degree), so prefer iteration to index loops.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/eliasfanographmodule\/eliasfanograph\/edges-swift.struct","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EliasFanoGraph.Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/EliasFanoGraphModule\/documentation\/EliasFanoGraphModule\/EliasFanoGraph\/Edges-swift.struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"}]}}}